<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc238560344" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario X: Three-level deep nested numbered list</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider an alarm escalation workflow where each stage contains additional details.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>nested</keyword>
        <keyword>numbered</keyword>
        <keyword>alarm</keyword>
        <keyword>Alarm</keyword>
        <keyword>Send</keyword>
        <keyword>notifications</keyword>
        <indexterm>nested</indexterm>
        <indexterm>numbered</indexterm>
        <indexterm>alarm</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody><section><p>Consider an alarm escalation workflow where each stage contains additional details.</p>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Three-level deep nested numbered list</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry> .md input </entry>
                     <entry> DITA output </entry>
                  </row>                  
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock># Alarm Escalation Workflow
  1. Alarm Detection
  - Evaluate alarm rules
  - Determine severity
  2. Notification Delivery
  - Send email notifications
  - Send SMS notifications
  3. Resolution</codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>&lt;concept id="alarm_escalation_workflow"&gt;     &lt;title&gt;Alarm Escalation Workflow&lt;/title&gt;     &lt;conbody&gt;         &lt;ol&gt;             &lt;li&gt;                 Alarm Detection                 &lt;ul&gt;                     &lt;li&gt;Evaluate alarm rules&lt;/li&gt;                     &lt;li&gt;Determine severity&lt;/li&gt;                 &lt;/ul&gt;             &lt;/li&gt;             &lt;li&gt;                 Notification Delivery                 &lt;ul&gt;                     &lt;li&gt;Send email notifications&lt;/li&gt;                     &lt;li&gt;Send SMS notifications&lt;/li&gt;                 &lt;/ul&gt;             &lt;/li&gt;             &lt;li&gt;Resolution&lt;/li&gt;         &lt;/ol&gt;     &lt;/conbody&gt; &lt;/concept&gt;</codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p>
            <b>Result:</b> The converter preserves both list levels. The numbered workflow stages become a DITA <codeph>&lt;ol&gt;</codeph>, while the nested bullet items become DITA <codeph>&lt;ul&gt;</codeph> elements within the corresponding list items.</p></section></refbody>
</reference>
